From d3c68739b5f9784ff7b9c93d3389261d42b7756b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:52:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm, VideoPlayer, settings: play HDR videos as SDR
 by choice

On a display that takes HDR, an HDR10, HDR10+ or HLG video always went
out as HDR: the only way to send it as SDR was to turn off Kodi's "Adjust
display HDR mode", which does it for every HDR video and for Dolby Vision
that is rebuilt as HDR10. "Play HDR videos as SDR" (System > Display,
expert level, Never by default) does it for HLG videos, or for HLG, HDR10
and HDR10+ videos: for a TV that shows HLG badly, or a projector whose SDR
picture is better than its HDR one.

Such a picture goes out as an SDR video does. SetHDR() takes it as SDR: no
HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA and no HDR10+ InfoFrame, and HDR signalling left from
before is taken away. VideoPlayer tells the change of mode of an SDR video.
The picture is mapped as on a display without HDR: by the bridge with the
tone mapping "Reference (BT.2390)" and the display of "HDR to SDR: the
display it is made for", by Kodi with its own methods. HDR10 adapted to the
display and HDR over the tunnel are not asked for it. Dolby Vision is not
affected, nor a video that a setting sends as Dolby Vision; "HLG as Dolby
Vision" on Automatic gives way to the choice, On does not. The setting is
taken when a video starts, and only where Kodi's HDR output is on and the
display takes HDR: with Never, and everywhere else, nothing changes.
kodi.log says it once a video. The player information heads such a video
"SDR, as chosen in the display settings", with a note that says where the
choice is made, instead of "the TV is not told this video is HDR". The
texts are in English and Spanish (es_es, es_ar, es_mx).

Tests on the host: the rule against a model (40 cases) and four mutants,
the page of the player information (and, without the choice, the same page
as before for 6048 inputs) with three mutants, and the wiring (14
places) with a mutant of each.
