 msgid "HDR on displays without Dolby Vision, and projectors"
 msgstr ""
 
+#. Hades: setting label "videoscreen.hadeshdrassdr"; translated in Estuary (#32590)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41110"
+msgid "Play HDR videos as SDR"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadeshdrassdr"; translated in Estuary (#32591)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41111"
+msgid "For a display whose HDR picture you like less than its SDR one: a TV that shows HLG badly, or a projector. The videos chosen here are sent as ordinary SDR instead of HDR, converted as for a display without HDR: with the tone mapping \"Reference (BT.2390)\" (the default), for the display chosen in \"HDR to SDR: the display it is made for\". The display stays in its SDR picture mode, as for the menus. Never (the default): HDR videos go out as HDR. HLG videos: only HLG, which TV broadcasts use. HLG, HDR10 and HDR10+ videos: all three. Dolby Vision videos are not affected, nor videos that a setting sends as Dolby Vision. Greyed out while \"Adjust display HDR mode\" (Player > Videos) is off: every HDR video then goes out as SDR already. Applies from the next video."
